  "body": "Ordinary CI and the registered lifecycle baseline now use published Builds 4.44.2 (`ae68c59bd2f4145a23ccf68c3711f98eaf62195f`) and Platform 1.3.0 (`338a6afc31850761f49c0de7d399266dd15cfe84`). This replaces the older tuple that refused the full Parties package composition before provisioning. The direct catalog, tool manifest and both immutable v2 executor references agree.\n\nThe proposal preserves incoming main `3e4367622764118fc2ad710ad1040994ae4cfa49`, including EventStore `f213e411`, all 15 isolated projects, all six independent jobs, real persistence/authorization assertions, diagnostic retention and lifecycle controls. Exact current graph assertions follow FrontComposer 4.7.6 and Memories 3.0.23 while all dated owner approvals, prior selection rows and the complete signoff-ledger prefix remain intact. Publisher and validation revisions remain independently pinned.\n\nActual local validation on the committed source:\n\n- Runtime-free preparation used the authenticated signed 4.44.2 executable and genuine Platform tag; four-manifest and generated-declaration checks passed.\n- Four affected Release/package projects built with zero warnings or errors.\n- 69 caller, 21 selection, 19 diagnostic/harness and 22 catalog-boundary cases passed with zero failures or skips.\n- 32 lifecycle/controller and seven strict-declaration Python controls, actionlint, whitespace, root-gitlink controls and locked commitlint 21.2.4 passed.\n\nThe first harness command named a nonexistent project and never executed tests; the corrected explicit project command passed. No product guard, test assertion or effective native/hold budget was relaxed.\n\nFull hosted CI, UI, native all-owner startup/wire/persistence/anonymous401, retained native/functional/lifecycle bodies and exact cleanup must still pass on this proposal. The three real manual lifecycle scenarios remain pending and are not dispatched by this change. Source/component results grant no candidate or whole-story acceptance.\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> <sup>[Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) is generating a summary for commit 434b8ac0efb9f798b6f8d29fd851fff490b97732. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->",
